-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CCFULL-ROM prediction input.  The lines are read in order; blank lines and
lines starting with # are skipped, and everything after line 16 is ignored.
Paths are relative to the project root.  The trained parameter box, energy
range, and experimental data come from the manifest of the model.

 1   model_id of the trained model (line 10 of emulator_train.in).
 2   training_root it was trained into (line 12 of emulator_train.in).
 3   worker processes; each loads its own copy of the model and of CCFULL.
 4   prediction mode: single (line 5), latin_hypercube (line 6), or table
     (line 7).
 5   single point: beta2,beta4,beta6,V0,r0,a0.  It may lie outside the box.
 6   Latin hypercube: number of points, seed.
 7   table of points: a CSV file with a header line and the columns
     beta2,beta4,beta6,v0,r0,a0 in this order.
 8   box of the Latin hypercube: training (the box of the model), or custom
     (lines 9-10), which may extend beyond it.
 9   custom bounds of beta2, beta4, beta6, as line 13 of emulator_train.in.
 10  custom bounds of V0, r0, a0, as line 14 of emulator_train.in.
 11  energies: experimental (the measured energies of the model's data), grid
     (line 12), or selected (line 13).  They must lie in the trained range.
 12  energy grid: first, last, step in MeV.
 13  selected energies in MeV; keep a value here even when it is not used.
 14  1 = yes, 0 = no: show the measured cross sections; check against exact
     Numerov CCFULL at the same points and energies; report exact time / ROM
     time (needs the check).
 15  output directory; every run writes a new timestamped directory in it.
 16  1 = yes, 0 = no: write cross_sections.csv, run_summary.json, and
     point_timings.csv (ROM and exact time of every point).
